TCC(1)                      User Commands                    TCC(1)

NAME
    tcc - Tiny C Compiler

SYNOPSIS
    tcc [options] [-o outfile] [-c] file...
    tcc [options] -run file [arguments...]

DESCRIPTION
    tcc compiles, assembles and links C programs. Without -c or -shared it
    produces an executable linked against the shared libraries in /lib.
    With -run it compiles the file into memory and runs it with the
    remaining arguments.

OPTIONS
    -c            compile to an object file
    -o file       write the output to file
    -shared       produce a shared object
    -run          compile and run
    -E            preprocess only
    -Dname[=v]    define a macro
    -Uname        undefine a macro
    -Idir         add an include directory
    -Ldir         add a library directory
    -lname        link with libname.so or libname.a
    -g            add debugging information
    -w            suppress warnings
    -Wall         enable warnings
    -v            print the version, twice for the search paths
    -static       link statically (libc.a is not installed)

FILES
    /usr/include            system headers
    /usr/lib/tcc/include    the compiler's own headers
    /usr/lib/tcc/libtcc1.a  runtime library
    /lib/crt1.o             C runtime start

SEE ALSO
    make(1), ar(1), tcc-doc in the tinycc sources
